{"seconds": 146.8, "exit": 0, "final": "After Kxg2, the knight on e5 is hanging. We play Qxe5 winning the knight. We're up a piece (knight = 3) minus the pawn (g2 = 1) that Black captured, net +2. That's winning for White.\n\nSo even the Qxg2+ line is good for White.\n\nAlright, I'm confident. Final answer:\n\n**Best move:** Qh5\n\n**Coaching note (75 words):**\nYour knight on e5 is overloaded\u2014it's only defended by your queen. White plays Qh5, attacking the knight and threatening f7. If you try Nf3+ to give check and escape, White responds gxf3 (pawn takes), and your queen is caught: Qg5+ is forced but White captures with Qxg5, winning your queen! The lesson: when a piece's only defender is your queen, watch for tactics that force it away.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Qh5\", \"line\": [\"Qh5\", \"Nf3+\", \"gxf3\", \"Qg5+\", \"Qxg5\", \"Kg7\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "r3k2r/pp3ppp/4p3/3qn3/8/8/P1P2PPP/R1BQ1RK1 w kq - 0 14"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "r3k2r/pp3ppp/4p3/3qn3/8/8/P1P2PPP/R1BQ1RK1 w kq - 0 14"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "r3k2r/pp3ppp/4p3/3qn3/8/8/P1P2PPP/R1BQ1RK1 w kq - 0 14"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-square_info", "args": {"fen": "r3k2r/pp3ppp/4p3/3qn3/8/8/P1P2PPP/R1BQ1RK1 w kq - 0 14", "square": "d5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-square_info", "args": {"fen": "r3k2r/pp3ppp/4p3/3qn3/8/8/P1P2PPP/R1BQ1RK1 w kq - 0 14", "square": "e5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r3k2r/pp3ppp/4p3/3qn3/8/8/P1P2PPP/R1BQ1RK1 w kq - 0 14", "move": "Qh5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r3k2r/pp3ppp/4p3/3qn3/8/8/P1P2PPP/R1BQ1RK1 w kq - 0 14", "move": "Qd4"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r3k2r/pp3ppp/4p3/3qn3/8/8/P1P2PPP/R1BQ1RK1 w kq - 0 14", "move": "Bg5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r3k2r/pp3ppp/4p3/3qn3/8/8/P1P2PPP